# JRE legs CI publishes beside the Dockerfile's default (TEMURIN_VERSION), each
# tagged <jena>-jre<major>. Read by build.yml's plan step and moved by
# upstream-check's bump PR; it is not a build input.
#
# One leg per line: <x64 version>, or <x64 version>/arm64=<arm64 version> while
# Adoptium has not built the x64 version for aarch64. Both must share a major.
# upstream-check drops the /arm64= part once aarch64 catches up.
#
# 25 is the current LTS. It is not the default because Jena 6.x targets 21 (the
# jar's manifest says Java-Version: 21), and moving the default changes what
# `6.2.0` and `latest` mean. The leg exists for extension jars built for release
# 22+ (java.lang.foreign is final from 22), which a 21 JVM refuses outright.
#
# LTS only, unless someone needs a feature release for a specific reason: a
# feature release gets Temurin builds for about six months, then no security
# updates at all.
25.0.5.1+2
